{
  "note": "Development hub path (ticket 26/09/23 U5, coordinator rule 23): an explicitly named hub is JOIN-ONLY (a serve waits with a localized status and gives up after a declared bound, never starts a hub); only the default hub is started, behind an owner lease per port and data root; the owner republishes a catalog the current hub cannot load. `roles`: explicit hub url → role. `locales`: POSIX locale variables → terminal language. `statuses`: every status and its exact en/de line. `leases`: records the lease reader accepts (`valid`) or refuses (`invalid`), which the schema `DevHubLeaseV1` must classify the same way. `catalogs`: a data root's trusted catalog (pointer + generation header) → freshness (`absent` / `current` / `stale` with the reason's leading words). `joins`: a fake hub that binds after `bindsAfterMs` (null: never) and the join bound → outcome. `owns`: the default-hub path under a lease state and port state → whether an owner is spawned, the status kinds reported, and the outcome. `serves`: the ONE shared serve fixture `ensureDevServe` (ticket 26/09/23 S18, R10 contract): `plans` port → plan; `spawns` a `DevServeSpawnRequestV1` (react or wgpu shell, dev or release) → the exact process it becomes; `invalidRequests` requests the schema refuses; `urls` a `--serve` url → its loopback port or a refusal; `statuses` every progress line en/de; `scenarios` real processes on a detect-port port: what was there before (`none` | `http` serve | `tcp` non-serve), how the started serve behaves (`bootsAfterMs`, null = never answers; `exits` = dies at once), an optional cancel and boot bound → reused, the status kinds reported, the error class, and whether the port is free after `stop()` (detect-port oracle).",
